"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:36
msgid ""
"fetches information about a store path in the HTTP binary cache located at "
"https://cache.nixos.org/, which is a type of store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:39
msgid ""
"Store URLs can specify **store settings** using URL query strings, i.e. by "
"appending `?name1=value1&name2=value2&...` to the URL. For instance,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:43
msgid ""
"```\n"
"--store ssh://machine.example.org?ssh-key=/path/to/my/key\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:47
msgid ""
"tells Nix to access the store on a remote machine via the SSH protocol, "
"using `/path/to/my/key` as the SSH private key. The supported settings for "
"each store type are documented below."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:51
msgid "`auto` special URL"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:53
msgid ""
"The special store URL `auto` causes Nix to automatically select a store as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:56
msgid ""
"Use the [local store](#local-store) `/nix/store` if `/nix/var/nix` is "
"writable by the current user."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:59
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if `/nix/var/nix/daemon-socket/socket` exists, [connect to the "
"Nix daemon listening on that socket](#local-daemon-store)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:62
msgid ""
"Otherwise, on Linux only, use the [local chroot store](../../store/types/"
"local-store.md#chroot) `~/.local/share/nix/root`, which will be created "
"automatically if it does not exist."
