#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:502
msgid ""
"This store is part of an [experimental feature](../../development/"
"experimental-features.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:144
msgid ""
"To use this store, make sure the [`local-overlay-store` experimental feature]"
"(../../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-local-overlay-store) "
"is enabled. For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:153
msgid "**Store URL format**: `local-overlay`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:155
msgid ""
"This store type is a variation of the \\[local store\\] designed to leverage "
"Linux's [Overlay Filesystem](https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/overlayfs."
"html) (OverlayFS for short). Just as OverlayFS combines a lower and upper "
"filesystem by treating the upper one as a patch against the lower, the local "
"overlay store combines a lower store with an upper almost-\\[local store\\]. "
"(\"almost\" because while the upper filesystems for OverlayFS is valid on "
"its own, the upper almost-store is not a valid local store on its own "
"because some references will dangle.) To use this store, you will first need "
"to configure an OverlayFS mountpoint [appropriately](#example-filesystem-"
"layout) as Nix will not do this for you (though it will verify the "
"mountpoint is configured correctly)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:160
msgid "Conceptual parts of a local overlay store"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:162
msgid ""
"_This is a more abstract/conceptual description of the parts of a layered "
"store, an authoritative reference. For more \"practical\" instructions, see "
"the worked-out example in the next subsection._"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:165
msgid "The parts of a local overlay store are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:167
msgid "**Lower store**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:169
msgid ""
"Specified with the [`lower-store`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-"
"lower-store) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:171
msgid ""
"This is any store implementation that includes a store directory as part of "
"the native operating system filesystem. For example, this could be a "
"\\[local store\\], \\[local daemon store\\], or even another local overlay "
"store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:174
msgid ""
"The local overlay store never tries to modify the lower store in any way. "
"Something else could modify the lower store, but there are restrictions on "
"this Nix itself requires that this store only grow, and not change in other "
"ways. For example, new store objects can be added, but deleting or modifying "
"store objects is not allowed in general, because that will confuse and "
"corrupt any local overlay store using those objects. (In addition, the "
"underlying filesystem overlay mechanism may impose additional restrictions, "
"see below.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:180
msgid ""
"The lower store must not change while it is mounted as part of an overlay "
"store. To ensure it does not, you might want to mount the store directory "
"read-only (which then requires the \\[read-only\\] parameter to be set to "
"`true`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:183
msgid "**Lower store directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:185
msgid "Specified with `lower-store.real` setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:187
msgid "This is the directory used/exposed by the lower store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:189
msgid ""
"As specified above, Nix requires the local store can only grow not change in "
"other ways. Linux's OverlayFS in addition imposes the further requirement "
"that this directory cannot change at all. That means that, while any local "
"overlay store exists that is using this store as a lower store, this "
"directory must not change."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:193
msgid "**Lower metadata source**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:195
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. A consequence of the `lower-store` setting, "
"depending on the type of lower store chosen."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:198
msgid ""
"This is abstract, just some way to read the metadata of lower store [store "
"objects](../../store/store-object.md). For example it could be a SQLite "
"database (for the \\[local store\\]), or a socket connection (for the "
"\\[local daemon store\\])."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:201
msgid ""
"This need not be writable. As stated above a local overlay store never tries "
"to modify its lower store. The lower store's metadata is considered part of "
"the lower store, just as the store's [file system objects](../../store/file-"
"system-object.md) that appear in the store directory are."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:205
msgid "**Upper almost-store**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:207
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. Instead the constituent parts are independently "
"specified as described below."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:210
msgid ""
"This is almost but not quite just a \\[local store\\]. That is because taken "
"in isolation, not as part of a local overlay store, by itself, it would "
"appear corrupted. But combined with everything else as part of an overlay "
"local store, it is valid."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:214
msgid "**Upper layer directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:216
msgid ""
"Specified with [`upper-layer`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-upper-"
"layer) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:218
msgid ""
"This contains additional [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) (or, "
"strictly speaking, their [file system objects](../../store/file-system-"
"object.md) that the local overlay store will extend the lower store with)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:221
msgid "**Upper store directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:223
msgid ""
"Specified with the [`real`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-real) "
"setting. This the same as the base local store setting, and can also be "
"indirectly specified with the [`root`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-"
"store-root) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:226
msgid "This contains all the store objects from each of the two directories."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:228
msgid ""
"The lower store directory and upper layer directory are combined via "
"OverlayFS to create this directory. Nix doesn't do this itself, because it "
"typically wouldn't have the permissions to do so, so it is the "
"responsibility of the user to set this up first. Nix can, however, "
"optionally check that the OverlayFS mount settings appear as expected, "
"matching Nix's own settings."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:232
msgid "**Upper SQLite database**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:234
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. The location of the database instead depends on the "
"[`state`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-state) setting. It is "
"always `${state}/db`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:238
msgid ""
"This contains the metadata of all of the upper layer [store objects](../../"
"store/store-object.md) (everything beyond their file system objects), and "
"also duplicate copies of some lower layer store object's metadata. The "
"duplication is so the metadata for the [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"closure) of upper layer [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) can be "
"found entirely within the upper layer. (This allows us to use the same SQL "
"Schema as the \\[local store\\]'s SQLite database, as foreign keys in that "
"schema enforce closure metadata to be self-contained in this way.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:245
msgid "Example filesystem layout"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:247
msgid ""
"Here is a worked out example of usage, following the concepts in the "
"previous section."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:249
msgid "Say we have the following paths:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:251
msgid "`/mnt/example/merged-store/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:253
msgid "`/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:255
msgid "`/mnt/example/store-b`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:257
msgid ""
"Then the following store URI can be used to access a local-overlay store at "
"`/mnt/example/merged-store`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:259
msgid ""
"```\n"
"local-overlay://?root=/mnt/example/merged-store&lower-store=/mnt/example/"
"store-a&upper-layer=/mnt/example/store-b\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:263
msgid ""
"The lower store directory is located at `/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store`, "
"while the upper layer is at `/mnt/example/store-b`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:265
msgid ""
"Before accessing the overlay store you will need to ensure the OverlayFS "
"mount is set up correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:267
msgid ""
"```shell\n"
"mount -t overlay overlay \\\n"
"  -o lowerdir=\"/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store\" \\\n"
"  -o upperdir=\"/mnt/example/store-b\" \\\n"
"  -o workdir=\"/mnt/example/workdir\" \\\n"
"  \"/mnt/example/merged-store/nix/store\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:275
msgid ""
"Note that OverlayFS requires `/mnt/example/workdir` to be on the same volume "
"as the `upperdir`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md:277
msgid ""
"By default, Nix will check that the mountpoint as been set up correctly and "
"fail with an error if it has not. You can override this behaviour by passing "
"[`check-mount=false`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-check-mount) "
"if you need to."
msgstr ""

